WEBVTT

00:00:01,490 --> 00:00:07,550
Hello everybody, this is Dr. Kevin Conner, it's time for our 60-second cancer update.

00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:11,430
This time we're going to talk about cancer and circadian rhythm.

00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:14,810
Several new studies have come out recently, I talked about it in our blog, so you want

00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:17,090
to more data, go to that.

00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:22,090
But our circadian rhythm is really our hormonal rhythm and how hormones are secreted in our

00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:23,090
body.

00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:25,810
They're affected by a lot of things.

00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:33,110
And the study showed that the more interruptions, or circadian rhythm disruptions that we have

00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:36,610
can lead to an increase incident of cancer.

00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:41,510
And for those who have cancer, an increase of the cancer cell growth, that was really an

00:00:41,510 --> 00:00:44,110
interesting piece of this last study.

00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:50,070
People that have cancer, that have numerous circadian rhythm disruptors in their life, increases

00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:51,910
the growth of cancer cells.

00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:55,710
You can see on the slide and pause it, you can see the different things that affect circadian

00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:56,710
rhythm.

00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:59,430
But we want to get to some things that you can do about it.

00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:03,870
Try to keep healthy sleep cycle is really a number one.

00:01:03,870 --> 00:01:08,170
Try to go to bed at the same time each night, try to live it screen time before bed so you

00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:13,470
can get to sleep, use natural sleep aids like melatonin if necessary, no matter if melatonin

00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:19,110
could be a great cancer help, learn ways to deal with stress and time management.

00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:24,550
Check also your drugs that you're taking for side effects because they can be a major disruptors

00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:26,550
in circadian rhythm.

00:01:26,550 --> 00:01:32,470
Schedule regular rest and nap times, avoid estrogens and other hormones in our environment.

00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:34,550
They can be major disruptors too.

00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:35,550
All right, great news.

00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,350
Talk to you next time.

